{
  "abstract": "No principal upper cone above a noncomputable Turing degree is order-isomorphic to the partially ordered set of all Turing degrees. The formalization adapts degree-coding, persistence, forcing, and generic representation arguments to a hypothetical cone isomorphism, and uses a Baire-category argument to rule out a nonzero cone base. No regularity assumption is imposed on the isomorphism.",
